    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Qwen3 dispatch, checkpoint mapping and per-head normalization",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "ARCHITECTURES derives the new record from Qwen3Model.config_class and Qwen3Config.arch_string. Config.from_directory selects that configuration class from the single architectures entry; Model.from_config subsequently constructs config.model_class. Unlike the thin Qwen2 wrapper, Qwen3Config explicitly passes its own model class to Config.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1da1a4c30fa6446bbc2b4ca8160d83b9",
              "call_701254c026304f409bb4dc24e34b11ab",
              "call_c1fb750872d64970aee0030b4f5055e2",
              "call_f074dbec87f240f79f9aade69e9c14e6",
              "call_d25418fff69f4937947467d013a8b025",
              "call_c00ec6fa1e444d80aa35912a5379a24a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Qwen3Config preserves the Llama configuration contract: explicit head_dim takes precedence over hidden_size // num_attention_heads; missing KV-head count defaults to query-head count; hidden_act may be absent but otherwise must be silu; intermediate width, layer count and RMS epsilon are required. Tied embeddings default to false. These fields feed the projection widths, block count, norms and head fallback in the new builder.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_701254c026304f409bb4dc24e34b11ab",
              "call_52cb84003c8c480380dc968df60e3abd",
              "call_f074dbec87f240f79f9aade69e9c14e6",
              "call_ac85d7bc5fbf45fcb99f33bf7c399a1f",
              "call_ce5f1544b78442d7a611b5a07d1c60ec",
              "call_8a125fae906f454dba167a3cf4d833ec",
              "call_372e58c4b0b344ddaf457792feadaca2",
              "call_8e2d62c92b81455d961e553a46d05f1c",
              "call_b4d91a7225874bdda09f5af1270185ff",
              "call_aed694873e64410aa9a30f6851f7ba99"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The module sequence is token embedding, one TransformerBlock per layer, final RMSNorm with half output, then the vocabulary projection. Each block maps input_layernorm, self_attn.{q,k,v,o}_proj, post_attention_layernorm and mlp.{gate,up,down}_proj. With residual width H, head width D, query heads Q, KV heads K and intermediate width I, the projection shapes are [QD,H], [KD,H], [KD,H], [H,QD], [I,H], [I,H] and [H,I]. The two added self_attn.{q,k}_norm weights have width D, not H or QD.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_701254c026304f409bb4dc24e34b11ab",
              "call_45190be9639444be8529a59e7cc3d564",
              "call_c8114d51ddf7483eb5437e5214836afe",
              "call_7ac6d10c8fa54e7ea078a1b914e42ff0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Attention registers both norms for loading and applies them after reshaping projections into individual heads, before RoPE, in SDPA, uncached FlashAttention and cached FlashAttention. V is not normalized. RMSNorm.forward flattens all leading axes into rows and invokes the native kernel, so the operation is per head: x\u00b7w/sqrt(mean(x\u00b2)+epsilon). Q/K outputs are explicitly half precision. The native wrapper requires half weights, matching last-axis width and width divisible by four; the reference head width 128 satisfies that width condition.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_45190be9639444be8529a59e7cc3d564",
              "call_c8114d51ddf7483eb5437e5214836afe",
              "call_b149b543f6374cd19d91e9582a935fea",
              "call_c8f8bbb799854e22a1d89ba87757d18b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The parent-tree q_norm search finds only Attention\u2019s optional implementation, not a model builder enabling it. Qwen3 therefore activates an existing capability. Reusing the generic RMSNorm kernel avoids another implementation, but its 1024-thread launch and existing specialization TODO do not establish efficient execution for 128-element heads.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2bca98f285864cb8826a83190074e14f",
              "call_701254c026304f409bb4dc24e34b11ab",
              "call_c8114d51ddf7483eb5437e5214836afe",
              "call_b149b543f6374cd19d91e9582a935fea"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All 17 inspected Qwen3 configs declare Qwen3ForCausalLM, D=128, K=8, SiLU, RMS epsilon 1e-6, vocabulary 151936, theta 1000000, null rope_scaling and disabled sliding-window attention. Thus their explicit settings, rather than the builder\u2019s missing-field fallbacks, determine these values. The unrestricted Attention defaults agree with these configs.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c8f8bbb799854e22a1d89ba87757d18b",
              "call_109c9d528a7a41d795103b7a9e3ca272",
              "call_854739b1cb7c4e4aaafd3fa1e3924c25",
              "call_888d4268550b465d8a74118b81a059aa",
